WEBVTT

00:00:08.170 --> 00:00:11.450
<i>He takes away children who don't want to become grown-ups. {has to change to fit}{## yeah sure}</i>

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:13.990
<i>He's a mischievous fairy. {## I can't believe I fucking missed this}</i>

00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.610
<i>I was invited as well. {## no reason for this to have to change, though, except maybe comma period}</i>

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:18.780
<i>By Peter. {## no reason for this to have to change, though, except maybe comma period}</i>

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:44.140
Peter...

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:45.550
Peter?

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:48.850
Wh-Wh-What are you doing here?!

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:51.330
I mean, I finished making this.

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.780
O-Oh, thanks.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:55.200
So, who's Pe—

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:01.330
What was that for?

00:01:01.330 --> 00:01:05.070
Oh, that's right! This is almost done, so could you finish it up?

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:08.220
If it's almost done, then just do it yourse—

00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:08.220
Don't be stingy! {## not a huge fan of 'stingy' in non-material contexts but apparently it's acceptable}

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.730
I already made all of these!

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:16.710
Well, I figured this might happen.

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:30.220
There's so much I wanted to talk to you about

00:01:24.810 --> 00:01:30.220
hanashitakatta koto takusan atta no ni

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:35.560
But my mind went blank when I saw your face

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:35.560
kao miru to wasurechau

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:44.170
Every time you peek in to pick me up after school my heart lights up

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:44.170
houkago mukae ni kitekureru no ga ureshikute

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:51.420
I wonder why I so hopelessly feel this way about you

00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:51.420
doushite kimi ja nakucha dame na no kana

00:01:56.910 --> 00:02:05.170
Maybe it's like how we can't live without the sun or sea

00:01:56.910 --> 00:02:05.170
taiyou ya mizu ga hitsuyou na no to niteru ki ga suru

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:12.560
The days have begun to get shorter now

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:12.560
hi ga mijikaku nattekita ne

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:20.690
Why must they cut off my time with you?

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:20.690
mou chotto issho ni itai no ni

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:26.300
Tomorrow and the day after, and every day forevermore

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:26.300
ashita mo asatte mo sono saki mo zutto

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:31.450
I want to keep walking home together like this

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:31.450
kouyatte kimi to kaeritai

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:36.900
No matter what the weather was, no matter how my day went

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:36.900
donna tenki demo donna kibun demo

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:44.670
The moment you raise your hand to wave goodbye

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:44.670
mata ne to kimi ga te wo furu toki

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:52.650
I feel like it has been a wonderful day

00:02:44.670 --> 00:02:52.650
ii hi datta to omoeru kara

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:12.800
Ane-chan-senpai!

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.590
We're here for collection! {## 'to collect'}

00:03:20.440 --> 00:03:21.380
She's asleep.

00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:24.220
What should we do now?

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:26.750
There are still a few left over.

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:27.720
Bitter melon juice

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:31.620
Guess we can wait until she wakes up for now.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:32.980
Good idea.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:40.590
So, you know how school feels kind of mysterious today?

00:03:40.590 --> 00:03:41.460
Yeah.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:45.320
I've been thinking that it kind of feels similar to Halloween. {## 'was ... felt' for the other one}

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:48.440
You mean like dreams and reality are mixed together?

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:49.040
Yeah.

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:53.000
I feel like we've unknowingly wandered into a dream.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.050
And dreaming is your specialty.

00:03:56.050 --> 00:03:58.960
<i>I can hear Pikari and Tekochin talking...</i>

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:04.210
Do you ever dream about wanting to run, but having your legs stuck in place?

00:04:04.210 --> 00:04:05.440
Sometimes.

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:10.220
I get all worked up about it trying to move, but then I just wake up exhausted.

00:04:10.570 --> 00:04:13.730
When that happens, you just have to use a prop.

00:04:13.730 --> 00:04:14.980
A prop?

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:17.210
Like a broom to help you fly.

00:04:17.210 --> 00:04:19.580
You can ride brooms?! It seems like they'd break.

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:22.580
They're not for riding, just sitting on.

00:04:22.580 --> 00:04:26.380
You're the one actually flying. It just helps you imagine it.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:26.290
<i>It sounds like a fairy tale.</i>

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:28.750
Oh, I think I get it!

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:30.120
<i>Like a witch teaching magic to her apprentice.</i>

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:33.960
Turn the broom left or right to turn. 
When you want to go up, just point it that way.

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.960
<i>It's a strange but comforting conversation. {## alt. 'strange, but comforting, conversation', one comma is wrongu}</i>

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:39.780
<i>I wish this time would go on for just a little longer.</i>

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:48.150
<i>It's him...</i>

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.330
<i>He's smiling like that again...</i>

00:04:57.400 --> 00:04:58.610
Peter!

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:02.990
Ane-chan-senpai?

00:05:27.060 --> 00:05:28.470
Ane-san...

00:05:29.690 --> 00:05:32.930
Blue... stripes...

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:38.600
Don't panic, Ane-san! You don't lose anything by being seen! {## you totally do, dude}

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:40.030
And yours aren't even that se— {## wait, how does he know?}

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.450
Why's she in such a rush?

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.850
I think she's running after someone.

00:05:48.850 --> 00:05:49.820
Someone?

00:05:49.820 --> 00:05:53.890
Yes. We thought she was fast asleep, but then she suddenly got up.

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:58.990
Huh? Is Ninomiya all right? {## why}

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:02.090
Yes, and she even ran off at full speed. {## really, why}

00:06:02.090 --> 00:06:03.410
I see.

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:14.440
He's gone.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.400
Hup...

00:06:36.950 --> 00:06:39.420
<i>He takes away children who don't want to become grown-ups.</i>

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:42.610
<i>He's a mischievous fairy. {## we gotta... spellcheck}</i>

00:06:52.230 --> 00:06:54.460
<i>I hate fairies like that.</i>

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:56.220
<i>But... {## or 'so', but I don't want to think too hard}</i>

00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.630
<i>Why do I want to meet him again so badly?</i>

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:11.490
<i>What's that light?</i>

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:22.380
Wasn't... it just nighttime?

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:28.270
What's going on?

00:07:31.990 --> 00:07:35.530
Did a water pipe burst somewhere? {## the usual word}

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:51.130
Huh? Where's all the school festival stuff?

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:56.620
Don't tell me I went back in time... {## why is this your first guess?}

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:01.080
<i>Everywhere I go is flooded.</i>

00:08:01.080 --> 00:08:03.520
<i>So why aren't any alarms sounding?</i>

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:08.750
<i>In fact, it's way too quiet.</i>

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:11.380
<i>There's not a single soul in sight. {## mind typo}</i>

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:19.180
For a dream... this seems a bit <i>too</i> well defined.

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:24.650
Dagashi

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:24.650
Candy

00:08:19.180 --> 00:08:24.650
Ice Cream

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:24.650
That candy store went out of business when I was in kindergarten. {## there's no need for this, dagashi aren't that weird}

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:27.110
Not to mention...

00:08:29.180 --> 00:08:31.320
That's a phone booth.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:33.520
I really did go back... {## doesn't read as a cutoff, so does read as 'back in', as in like, once more unto the breach}

00:08:38.430 --> 00:08:40.870
Oh, a lost child. {gender neutral lost boys}{## why do you figure this wasn't the standard 'mayoigo'?}{when given the chance, always maximize references}

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:44.580
<i>Huh?</i>

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:50.000
E-Excuse me, was there an 
evacuation drill or something today?

00:08:50.720 --> 00:08:53.010
You should return home soon.

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:54.590
<i>What's this?</i>

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:56.930
<i>Her voice...</i>

00:08:57.380 --> 00:09:00.390
<i>Though she's a little—no, a </i>lot<i> younger...</i>

00:09:00.820 --> 00:09:02.350
<i>No way...</i>

00:09:02.820 --> 00:09:05.310
Hey, wait a second!

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:07.270
Mato-chan!

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:13.570
<i>Yeah, there's no way it'd be her.</i>

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:18.030
How do you know my name?

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:20.170
<i>Bingo out of nowhere!</i>

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:22.400
I don't know who you are.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.500
U-Um...

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:31.210
You don't seem to be one of the usual lost children.

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:33.750
Fine, come with me.

00:09:33.750 --> 00:09:35.670
O-Okay. {## did somebody forget to draw her hair}

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:43.350
Want one?

00:09:43.710 --> 00:09:45.890
Th-Thank you.

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:46.810
No problem.

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:49.770
I prefer coffee, anyway.

00:09:50.680 --> 00:09:53.230
<i>It really is Mato-chan-sensei.</i>

00:09:54.120 --> 00:09:59.160
<i>The entire city is flooded, and we're the only people here.</i>

00:09:59.160 --> 00:10:00.950
<i>This has to be a dream.</i>

00:10:00.950 --> 00:10:02.550
We're inside a dream.

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:04.590
Whose?

00:10:05.280 --> 00:10:09.330
This is the inside of a baby's dream.

00:10:14.410 --> 00:10:17.590
A baby who was abandoned alone at a shrine.

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:22.560
The only thing a powerless baby can do is to dream. {## well, and cry}

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:27.210
Within a neverending dream, he can live forever.

00:10:28.230 --> 00:10:32.940
That is how the world we're in right now began.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.610
So...

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:38.360
Do you want to hear more?

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:41.370
Please.

00:10:42.850 --> 00:10:44.120
You're a strange one.

00:10:44.440 --> 00:10:47.080
I think we'll get along. Cheers.

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:57.800
As the baby lived on inside his dream, 
a bizarre phenomenon began to occur.

00:10:58.710 --> 00:11:04.750
Humans dreaming in the real world 
started to get lost inside the baby's.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:12.730
And those are the lost children, like us?

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:18.050
The ages, genders, and even original years of the lost children vary greatly. {## orig. 'age the lost children come from', same 'gender'}

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:22.730
And each one induces a significant change in the baby.

00:11:29.370 --> 00:11:35.130
As the baby watched and listened to the lost children's information, memories, and experiences,

00:11:35.630 --> 00:11:39.810
he became able to age himself within the dream.

00:11:40.930 --> 00:11:46.260
And his world, at first limited only to the shrine, slowly began to expand at his will.

00:11:49.180 --> 00:11:51.690
Well, it's up to you to choose whether to believe or not. {## MATO'S BELIEVE IT OR NOT}

00:11:54.880 --> 00:11:58.110
How did you learn all that insider information, Mato-chan?

00:11:58.110 --> 00:11:59.740
I asked the baby himself.

00:12:00.900 --> 00:12:04.690
<i>Oh, no... This is all way too absurd.</i>

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.360
Be careful. {## this scene is COOL AS FUCK HOLY SHIT}

00:12:38.570 --> 00:12:41.280
I see. So that's where you are,

00:12:41.720 --> 00:12:42.880
Peter.

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:45.740
Huh? Did you say "Peter"?

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:50.990
Ever since he was a baby, he has been dreaming of this world.

00:12:51.710 --> 00:12:55.420
Yes, of this land of eternity...

00:12:56.150 --> 00:12:57.800
Peter's Neverland.

00:13:13.760 --> 00:13:15.890
We managed to finish them all off...

00:13:16.260 --> 00:13:18.160
We can finally go back.

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:23.410
Ane-chan-senpai still hasn't come back.

00:13:23.410 --> 00:13:24.280
Yeah.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:28.970
I wonder who Peter is.

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:31.990
{=3}Days left until School Festival

00:13:25.740 --> 00:13:31.990
{=2}Final spurt!!

00:13:29.800 --> 00:13:30.950
Peter?

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:31.990
Do you know anything?

00:13:31.990 --> 00:13:36.260
I think he's the one she went looking for.

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:38.890
That was the name she said earlier, right?

00:13:38.890 --> 00:13:39.730
Yeah.

00:13:43.110 --> 00:13:44.490
Advisor Cha!

00:13:45.630 --> 00:13:47.880
Huh? A drink box?

00:13:50.300 --> 00:13:53.810
You brought it here for us? Thanks!

00:13:53.810 --> 00:14:00.310
Strawberry Milk

00:13:54.200 --> 00:13:59.170
Oh, Advisor Cha! Have you seen Ane-chan-senpai anywhere?

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:06.970
Let's follow him.

00:14:06.970 --> 00:14:07.780
Okay.

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:23.340
The first time I met Peter

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:26.340
was the day of my middle school graduation. {## the time itself is the day / that is a -short- skirt}

00:14:31.540 --> 00:14:35.310
I wish things could've stayed the same a while longer.

00:14:49.850 --> 00:14:50.950
Nice to meet you.

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:58.940
After that, I visited this world 
countless times through my dreams. {## 'several' is so... well-defined and smol}

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:02.840
He seemed happy every time.

00:15:03.440 --> 00:15:09.570
Since he didn't have a name, I suggested the one of the protagonist of my favorite story.

00:15:09.570 --> 00:15:11.050
And that was "Peter".

00:15:12.800 --> 00:15:17.420
All right, what now? Assuming Peter is on that ship...

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:20.690
We'll have to give up.

00:15:21.580 --> 00:15:24.150
This is a dream world, isn't it?

00:15:24.150 --> 00:15:24.730
Yeah.

00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:29.190
In that case, I know a way we can get up there.

00:15:33.630 --> 00:15:39.160
Listen, the broom is just for steering! It's only for sitting on!

00:15:41.180 --> 00:15:44.230
Where did you learn how to fly?! {## it sounds like Mato's got road rage, but if you like / 'How do you know how to fly?!'}{she's only shouting incidentally}

00:15:44.230 --> 00:15:46.160
My underclassman—

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:50.670
I know a professional dreamer!

00:15:51.140 --> 00:15:56.350
I overheard her talking about how to do this earlier!

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:58.350
D-Did you now?

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:10.730
Water is overflowing from the ship.

00:16:10.730 --> 00:16:11.740
That's right.

00:16:12.180 --> 00:16:18.990
According to Peter, the water's been pouring out continuously since Neverland was created.

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:24.160
And because of that, this world has always been in grave danger.

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:27.980
Look.

00:16:31.220 --> 00:16:33.840
The city is being flooded. {## maybe if you didn't park your ship right on top of it, dude}

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:36.550
At this rate, this world...

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:38.750
will be completely shut off.

00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:41.980
Nobody will ever...

00:16:42.330 --> 00:16:43.620
be able to come again. {## i mean that's fine, right?}

00:16:49.790 --> 00:16:52.280
Can't we stop the water somehow?

00:16:53.100 --> 00:16:54.490
<i>Mato-chan!</i>

00:16:57.650 --> 00:17:00.320
I thought up a way to save this world!

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:01.700
Huh?

00:17:02.290 --> 00:17:08.570
If we can't stop the water from falling down, all we need to do is expand its vessel, the world itself! {## kono sekai this, kono sekai that}

00:17:09.250 --> 00:17:15.260
I'll go out into the real world myself and bring lots of people over here!

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:19.070
What are you saying, Peter?!

00:17:19.070 --> 00:17:22.220
There's no helping people getting lost in dreams and wandering in here, {## 'no helping people' meaning 'cannot assist', not 'can do nothing about' / prescriptively, 'people's getting'}

00:17:22.220 --> 00:17:28.900
but you can't just intentionally draw strangers into a dream world that could close off at any time!

00:17:32.560 --> 00:17:36.740
Mato-chan, do you think this world should be closed off forever?

00:17:36.740 --> 00:17:40.560
Of course not! I'd never want that!

00:17:40.560 --> 00:17:42.540
But even if it happened—

00:17:43.900 --> 00:17:45.500
I understand now.

00:17:45.500 --> 00:17:46.500
Peter?

00:17:47.160 --> 00:17:51.080
Since you're just a stranger, never come back here again.

00:17:51.750 --> 00:17:53.670
<i>A... stranger?</i>

00:17:57.770 --> 00:17:59.260
Wait, Peter...

00:17:59.260 --> 00:18:00.870
Peter!

00:18:04.980 --> 00:18:12.190
Since then, no matter how many times I've 
come here, Peter hasn't shown himself once. {## so like, does Mato just dream these dreams on the reg? and always as her high school self?}

00:18:12.190 --> 00:18:14.250
But I need to see him again—

00:18:16.090 --> 00:18:22.030
There's something I wasn't able to say back then that I have to tell him!

00:18:24.070 --> 00:18:25.120
I found you,

00:18:25.510 --> 00:18:26.510
Peter.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:29.750
Did you lead her here?

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:32.220
I guess I can't blame you. {## egh, well}

00:18:34.700 --> 00:18:37.270
Hey, Ai. Looks like we meet again.

00:18:37.270 --> 00:18:38.430
Peter...

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:41.640
It's been quite some time since I've seen you, Mato-chan.

00:18:41.640 --> 00:18:42.890
Peter!

00:18:42.890 --> 00:18:45.350
There's no need to yell, Mato-chan.

00:18:45.980 --> 00:18:48.150
There's something I want to show you two.

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:50.810
Follow me.

00:19:04.880 --> 00:19:07.240
I thought we went inside the ship...

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:10.500
A shrine?

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:16.390
Yes.

00:19:17.130 --> 00:19:22.050
This is where everything in Neverland originated. {## ew, that cat is creepy}{cait sidhe isn't creepy}

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:28.640
Is this where the baby Peter is sleeping?

00:19:29.300 --> 00:19:32.980
As you can see, there's no stopping the overflowing water.

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:37.820
Since parting from you, I've visited the real world countless times. {## 'part with' is to give away, 'part from' being to separate for equals}

00:19:38.170 --> 00:19:43.830
But no matter how much I expanded this world, an even greater amount of water would follow. {## is it a rock?}{he's frozen in time}

00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:49.420
Neverland will soon meet its end.

00:19:51.510 --> 00:19:55.900
I'll stop inviting strangers to this world.

00:19:56.580 --> 00:19:59.490
Okay. That's for the best.

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:06.340
Now then, the two of you should leave as soon as possible.

00:20:07.550 --> 00:20:08.640
No.

00:20:09.160 --> 00:20:10.230
Mato-chan...

00:20:12.810 --> 00:20:16.310
Even after this, I'll come as much as I want.

00:20:16.820 --> 00:20:19.330
You have a place to call home.

00:20:20.860 --> 00:20:24.700
You might be trapped in this world forever.

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:27.070
I know that!

00:20:28.460 --> 00:20:33.940
But even if that happens, I alone will stay by your side.

